# Words of Wind activated twice makes two effects, each used up by one draw: "if multiple Words have been used prior to
# drawing a card, then you can choose which one to apply (and use up) each time you draw a card" (its ruling; CR 616.1).
# Bot1 activates it twice on turn 3 and casts Ancestral Recall: its first draw is replaced by one effect (Bot1 is asked which
# - they are alike), its second by the other, and its third is drawn. Each replacement has each player return a permanent:
# Bot1 its Mox Jet and then its Sol Ring, Bot2 its Swamp and then nothing, having none left (nobody asks a player with no
# permanent to choose one).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Sol Ring
Black Lotus
Words of Wind
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Plains
Ancestral Recall
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Words of Wind.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Words of Wind.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Words of Wind.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Replace(Words of Wind)
Bot1.Choose(Mox Jet)
Bot2.Choose(Swamp)
Bot1.Choose(Sol Ring)
! Bot2.Choose
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Plains; Mox Jet; Sol Ring; Island
Bot1.Library.Count = 19
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Mox Sapphire; Words of Wind
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
